(A) sign-flip control (G(1.4), k = (2.6, 0.1, -0.4), c = 0): relative residual of the weak translation system
  sigma = +1 x (eps/2) v v : max residual 8.59e-16
  sigma = -1 x (eps/2) v v : max residual 7.15e-02

(B) rigidity of the boost scalar sector: null space of the weak boost operator (unknowns X(6), Y(6))
  operator 8 x 12, rank 8; null-space dimension 4; max |X_T component| over null vectors = 2.2e-15; max |Y_qq component| = 2.1e-16
  (null directions are X_L, Y_T (constraint-proportional) and gauge combinations; X_T and Y_qq are fixed)

(C) strong closure (every component, no constraint-proportional terms), translation sector:
  random qhat: max residual 2.1e-11;  at qhat.v = 2.3e-02: |A_T| = 8.06e+01, |B_vL| = 6.97e+01
  random qhat: max residual 7.0e-11;  at qhat.v = 2.3e-03: |A_T| = 8.73e+02, |B_vL| = 7.57e+02
  random qhat: max residual 3.2e-11;  at qhat.v = 2.3e-04: |A_T| = 8.79e+03, |B_vL| = 7.63e+03
  strong closure needs A_T, B_vL ~ 1/(qhat.v): unbounded on the sphere -> only weak closure (with
  constraint-proportional terms, i.e. matter-dependent structure functions or field-dependent lapse/shift) is in class C.

(D) factorisation Phi_c = delta_c * Xi (Xi independent of c): compare B_c/delta_c, A_c/delta_c for c = 0, 1
  S(1.4) k=[1.6 1.6 0. ]: max relative difference of Phi_c/delta_c between c=0 and c=1: 3.2e-15
  G(1.4) k=[ 2.3 -1.9  0.7]: max relative difference of Phi_c/delta_c between c=0 and c=1: 7.2e-15
  G(1.4) k=[1.6 1.6 0. ]: max relative difference of Phi_c/delta_c between c=0 and c=1: 4.2e-15
  => {P_c^tot, P_d^tot} = 0 at degree 3 (antisymmetric delta_c delta_d cancels), and Phi_c = {P_c^0, W}
     with W = -i sum E.Xi_E f + h.Xi_h f: (beta) is the first-order canonical relocation of a system with bare P^0.
